he one end to the other.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And he overlaid the boards with gold, and made their rings of gold to be places for the bars, and overlaid the bars with gold.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book§chapter$«first_verse#ªlast_verse$¦verses’„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd he made a vail of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: with cherubims made he it of cunning work.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And he made thereunto four pillars of shittim wood, and overlaid them with gold: their hooks were of gold; and he cast for them four sockets of silver.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book§chapter$«first_verse%ªlast_verse&¦verses’„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd he made an hanging for the tabernacle door of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, of needlework;¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand the five pillars of it with their hooks: and he overlaid their chapiters and their fillets with gold: but their five sockets were of brass.¦layout ªlast_verse&